WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.538
IEC 62443 is a family of standards for industrial automation and control system

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:06.372
cybersecurity.

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:10.000
It connects organizational programs, risk assessment, system architecture,

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.720
product capabilities, service responsibilities, and lifecycle operation.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.320
It is not a single checklist or product.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.440
Responsibilities are shared but must remain explicit.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.920
Asset owners define risk and sustain the program.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.395
Integrators implement and verify secure systems.

00:00:23.395 --> 00:00:27.122
Product suppliers provide secure development practices and component capabilities.

00:00:27.122 --> 00:00:30.915
Service providers maintain access and changes within approved controls.

00:00:30.915 --> 00:00:33.320
Zones group assets with related security requirements.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:36.240
Conduits control communication between those zones.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.770
Security levels translate risk into protection expectations,

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:43.270
while the foundational requirements organize identity, use, integrity, confidentiality,

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:47.175
restricted flow, event response, and availability objectives.

00:00:47.175 --> 00:00:50.620
Successful implementation depends on evidence and engineering.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:54.225
Inventory assets, understand the process, assess risk, configure capabilities,

00:00:54.225 --> 00:00:58.700
test controls, govern remote access, monitor meaningful activity, maintain backups,

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:02.395
control changes, and plan for incident recovery and technology retirement.

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:05.160
The central lesson is collaboration across the lifecycle.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:09.605
IEC 62443 gives engineering, operations, cybersecurity, suppliers,

00:01:09.605 --> 00:01:13.065
and management a common structure for making defensible decisions.

00:01:13.065 --> 00:01:17.275
The official standards and environment-specific analysis provide the detail;

00:01:17.275 --> 00:01:20.800
disciplined ownership turns that detail into resilient industrial operations.
